From: Christopher Griffin <christophergriffin05@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 14:19:01 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 15/66] ipq40xx: w-118: light the radio LEDs

The 2.4 GHz, 5 GHz and scanning-radio LEDs had no trigger. Phy numbers
follow the order the radios were first found in, so board.d cannot
name them. A hotplug script ties each LED to its radio by device path
instead, with the radio's phyNradio trigger: the LED is lit while the
radio is enabled, as on the Arista C-360, C-260 and W-318.

Tested on a unit: the three LEDs follow the IPQ4019's two radios and
the QCA9882 card.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Christopher Griffin <christophergriffin05@gmail.com>
---
 .../hotplug.d/ieee80211/12-arista-w-118-leds  | 28 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 28 insertions(+)
 create mode 100755 target/linux/ipq40xx/base-files/etc/hotplug.d/ieee80211/12-arista-w-118-leds

diff --git a/target/linux/ipq40xx/base-files/etc/hotplug.d/ieee80211/12-arista-w-118-leds b/target/linux/ipq40xx/base-files/etc/hotplug.d/ieee80211/12-arista-w-118-leds
new file mode 100755
index 0000000000..7f968d5f63
--- /dev/null
+++ b/target/linux/ipq40xx/base-files/etc/hotplug.d/ieee80211/12-arista-w-118-leds
@@ -0,0 +1,28 @@
+#!/bin/sh
+# Arista W-118: each radio LED follows its radio, found by device path.
+# Phy numbers follow the order the radios were first found in. 2.4 and 5
+# are the IPQ4019's own radios, the third is the QCA9882 card on pcie0.
+# "phyNradio" lights the LED while the radio is enabled.
+
+[ "$ACTION" = add ] || exit 0
+
+. /lib/functions.sh
+
+[ "$(board_name)" = arista,w-118 ] || exit 0
+
+case "$(readlink "/sys/class/ieee80211/$DEVICENAME/device")" in
+*/a000000.wifi)
+	led=green:wlan-2ghz
+	;;
+*/a800000.wifi)
+	led=green:wlan-5ghz
+	;;
+*/0000:01:00.0)
+	led=green:wlan
+	;;
+*)
+	exit 0
+	;;
+esac
+
+echo "${DEVICENAME}radio" > "/sys/class/leds/$led/trigger"
